{"school":{"dbn":"20K062","name":"J.H.S. 062 Ditmas","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"20","district_label":"District 20","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":872,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"700 CORTELYOU ROAD, BROOKLYN, NY 11218","phone":"718 836 4630","website":"www.ditmas.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63343","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Our Vision is to cultivate a diverse community that is inclusive of a multi-cultural environment that fosters parent communication and strong family ties. Together, we achieve collaboration between teachers, administrators, and staff to provide rigorous instruction and college readiness to meet the needs of the 21st century child. Our mission is very simple: Our school's pride is the academic achievements of our students. Our motivation for working hard is their success. Lighting up the path for their future is in our hands. Our building consists of the 6th, 7th, and 8th grade academies. Throughout the course of our student's three years, they are introduced to the arts, and language. We offer all Common Core classes with curriculum that is standards-based and at grade level.  We provide an inclusive environment where all students receive quality instruction.  Ditmas has two Superintendent classes and two Algebra classes that are screened through the district. Ditmas is known for its media classes, where students are given the opportunity to work with the most advanced forms of new technology.  Afterschool programs are offered throughout the year. Our Title III and Title I programs offer academic help taught by Ditmas teachers. Here, at Ditmas, our students are challenged academically and appreciated for their cultural diversities.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"B, Q to Cortelyou Rd; F to Ditmas Av","bus":"B103, B35, B67, B68, B69, B8, BM1, BM2, B